  "query_preview": "out farther. At this point, it doesn't look like there\nwill be high near surface concentrations of smoke, so have not\nadded it into the weather grids. Hopefully the smoke stays mostly\nabove the surface this go around. \n\n- Izzi\n\nWednesday onward...\n\nHigh pressure will largely remain in control of our sensible \nweather through much of the work week yielding dry and more \ncomfortable conditions, particularly Wednesday and Thursday. The \nmoist and instability axis will start to build back towards the \nregion Thursday afternoon into Friday, and there's a signal for\none or several disturbances embedded within the northwest flow \naloft to pivot across the Great Lakes region. This may yield the\nnext chances for showers and thunderstorms, which may linger \ninto Saturday before another cold front arrives during the \nSaturday night/Sunday timeframe. \n\nCarlaw",
